  "headline_findings": {
    "K_band_recovery": "Null-selectivity at p99 recovers the 17-19% conserved-fraction band on Pythia 160M (18.1%) and Pythia 410M (18.5%) \u2014 independent validation of the K=0.18\u00d7n rule on the natural-text panel.",
    "K_band_does_NOT_generalize": "1B-class fractions vary 4.7%-27.3% under the same rule; conservation is within-Pythia-natural-text, not cross-architecture.",
    "T_50x_validates_across_1B_panel": "Direct per-model ablation-floor sweep on the three 1B models confirms 50\u00d7 is defensible: tight for Pythia 1B (catches 94% of effect; T* between 10x-30x), exactly right for OLMoE (T* = 30-50x, plateau at 4 heads), conservative for OLMo 1B (T* = 100x; only 2 heads suffice).",
    "olmo_1b_minimum_circuit_is_2_heads": "OLMo 1B's full causal induction circuit saturates at 2 heads (\u2265100x). Adding heads from 3 to 20 produces no additional drop.",
    "olmoe_plateau": "OLMoE selectivity at \u226530x, \u226550x = same 4 heads. Any threshold in 30-100\u00d7 returns the same circuit \u2014 strongest signature of a well-separated circuit in the panel.",
    "pythia_1b_bos_suppression": "Pythia 1B matched-random ablation of 6-11 random heads in the L4-L8 layers RAISES top-1 above baseline (16.7% at N=6, 36.1% at N=11 vs. 4.05% baseline). Reading: random ablation in those layers removes BOS-attractor heads that suppress induction; releasing the suppression brings induction performance to ~36%. Same pattern as the \u00a77.10 Pythia VB interferer finding (BOS-class heads suppressing the actual computation). Magnitude is largest in Pythia 1B; mild echo in OLMoE; absent in OLMo 1B.",
    "cross_model_T_star_variation": "T* varies by ~10x across the three 1B models. Reading: different models implement induction at different granularities \u2014 OLMo 1B uses 2 extremely sharp specialists (\u2265100\u00d7), OLMoE uses 4 mid-selectivity heads (30-200\u00d7 range), Pythia 1B distributes across 6+ multi-role heads (some in the 10-50\u00d7 band)."
  }
